          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Mr Ding asked ChatGPT for a good exam question. It said:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p97-q90-quotation",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "“The GCD of three numbers is 42 and their LCM is 16 800.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two of the numbers are 294 and 210. What could the third number be?”",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p97-q90-task",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He tried to work it out but found that this question is impossible. Explain why.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$16\\,800$ is not divisible by $294$, so it cannot be the LCM of a set containing $294$.",
      "worked": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p97-q90-answer",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{align*}\\text{HCF: }42&=2\\cdot3\\cdot7\\\\\\text{LCM: }16\\,800&=2^{5}\\cdot3\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7\\\\294&=2\\cdot3\\cdot7^{2}\\\\210&=2\\cdot3\\cdot5\\cdot7\\end{align*}",
                "display": true,
                "colour": "#268cff"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p97-q90-answer-reason",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The LCM must contain the largest power of each prime factor. Since 294 contains ",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "7^{2}",
                "display": false,
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", the LCM must be divisible by ",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "7^{2}",
                "display": false,
                "colour": "#268cff"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p97-q90-answer-conclusion",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But 16 800 has only one factor of 7, so it is not divisible by 294. Therefore, it cannot be the LCM of a set of numbers including 294.",
                "marks": [],
                "colour": "#268cff"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
